<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Specialist Letter</title>
    <style>
        * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
            font-size: 12pt;
            line-height: 1.6;
            padding: 40px 50px;
            background: white;
            color: #333;
            max-width: 210mm;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .letterhead {
            text-align: center;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #2d5016;
            padding-bottom: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }
        .letterhead h1 { color: #2d5016; font-size: 18pt; margin-bottom: 5px; }
        .letterhead .subtitle { color: #4a5568; font-size: 11pt; }
        .letterhead .contact { font-size: 9pt; color: #718096; margin-top: 10px; }
        .letter-info { margin-bottom: 25px; }
        .letter-info p { margin-bottom: 3px; }
        .recipient { margin-bottom: 25px; }
        .recipient p { margin-bottom: 2px; }
        .salutation { margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .patient-box {
            background: #f7fafc;
            border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
            padding: 15px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .patient-box h3 { font-size: 11pt; color: #2d5016; margin-bottom: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; }
        .patient-box table { width: 100%; font-size: 10pt; }
        .patient-box td { padding: 2px 10px 2px 0; }
        .patient-box td:first-child { font-weight: bold; width: 120px; }
        .content p { margin-bottom: 15px; text-align: justify; }
        .content h4 { color: #2d5016; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 11pt; }
        .content ul { margin-left: 25px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
        .content li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
        .signature { margin-top: 40px; }
        .signature .name { font-weight: bold; }
        .signature .credentials { font-size: 10pt; color: #4a5568; }
        .cc { margin-top: 30px; font-size: 10pt; color: #718096; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="letterhead">
        <h1>GASTROENTEROLOGY SPECIALISTS</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">Digestive Health & Endoscopy Services</div>
        <div class="contact">
            Suite 201, Specialist Medical Centre | 456 Collins Street, Melbourne VIC 3000<br>
            Phone: (03) 9666 2345 | Fax: (03) 9666 2346
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="letter-info">
        <p class="date">7 January 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="recipient">
        <p><strong>Dr Sarah Mitchell</strong></p>
        <p>Mitchell Family Practice</p>
        <p>45 Clinic Road</p>
        <p>Suburb VIC 3000</p>
    </div>

    <div class="salutation">
        <p>Dear Dr Mitchell,</p>
    </div>

    <div class="patient-box">
        <h3>Patient Information</h3>
        <table>
            <tr><td>Patient Name:</td><td>David BROWN</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Date of Birth:</td><td>22/07/1965 (60 years)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>UR Number:</td><td>MRN-1938472</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Procedure Date:</td><td>7 January 2026</td></tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="content">
        <p>Thank you for referring Mr Brown for surveillance colonoscopy. I performed the procedure today at Endoscopy Day Centre and provide the following report.</p>

        <h4>Procedure Summary</h4>
        <p>Colonoscopy was performed under conscious sedation with midazolam 4mg and fentanyl 75mcg. The bowel preparation was satisfactory. The colonoscope was advanced to the caecum, with photo documentation of the appendiceal orifice and ileocaecal valve.</p>

        <h4>Findings</h4>
        <p>Two sessile polyps were identified in the sigmoid colon:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>8mm polyp at 25cm - removed by hot snare polypectomy</li>
            <li>5mm polyp at 30cm - removed by cold snare polypectomy</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Both polyps were retrieved and sent for histopathological examination. The remainder of the colon was unremarkable with no other lesions identified.</p>

        <h4>Histopathology Results</h4>
        <p>Results confirm both lesions are tubular adenomas with low-grade dysplasia. Margins are clear. No evidence of malignancy.</p>

        <h4>Background History</h4>
        <p>Mr Brown has a history of Barrett's oesophagus diagnosed in 2022, currently on PPI therapy. His last gastroscopy was in January 2024 showing stable Barrett's segment without dysplasia.</p>

        <h4>Recommendations</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Continue Esomeprazole 40mg daily for Barrett's oesophagus</li>
            <li>Surveillance colonoscopy in 3 years (January 2029)</li>
            <li>Gastroscopy for Barrett's surveillance in 2 years (January 2028)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Mr Brown tolerated the procedure well and was discharged home in a stable condition with standard post-polypectomy instructions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="signature">
        <p class="name">Dr Sarah Williams</p>
        <p class="credentials">MBBS, FRACP, PhD</p>
        <p class="credentials">Consultant Gastroenterologist</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cc">
        <p>CC: Patient</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
